Upstream checks
===============

This folder tracks workarounds we carry for upstream bugs (broken package
builds, stale tests, regressions) and gives each one a script that probes
whether upstream has fixed the problem yet.  When a probe reports that the
upstream path is clear, the matching workaround in our configuration can be
removed.

Run the whole sweep from the dev shell:

    upstream-check

This iterates every check script in this folder, runs its probe, and prints a
summary listing which workarounds can now be dropped.

Each check is a single executable shell script (`*.sh`) in this folder.  The
runner treats the script's exit code as the verdict:

    0   workaround still required (upstream still broken)
    1   upstream path clear -> the workaround can be dropped
    2   inconclusive / probe error

A script should print a short, human-readable explanation of what it probed and
what to do, then exit with one of those codes.  Scripts may assume `git`, `jq`
and `nix` are on PATH (the dev shell provides them) and that the working tree is
the repository root, which they can locate with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`.

Adding a new check
------------------

When you add a workaround somewhere in the configuration, drop a sibling script
here named after the package, e.g. `foo.sh`.  Probe the real thing the
workaround exists to dodge -- usually "does upstream build with its tests
enabled" -- and report the verdict via the exit codes above.  No registration
is needed; the runner picks up every `*.sh` automatically.

`example.sh.template` is a commented stub covering the contract and the common
probe shapes.  Copy it, do not run it in place:

    cp example.sh.template <package>.sh && chmod +x <package>.sh

Current checks
--------------

    fpdf2.sh
        fpdf2 2.8.9's test_image_with_explicit_dimensions compares its output
        against a reference PDF generated with Pillow 12; Pillow 13 changes PNG
        decoding, so the generated bytes (6732d6d8...) no longer match the 2.8.9
        reference (c7b6e70b...) and checkPhase fails (py-pdf/fpdf2#2085,
        NixOS/nixpkgs#580380).  Workaround: the flake.nix overlay overrides
        python313's fpdf2 and copies the 2.9.0 reference (upstream 597cfff) over
        the 2.8.9 one while fpdf2 < 2.9.0 and Pillow is 13.x.  nixpkgs
        release-26.05 instead deselects the test (NixOS/nixpkgs#580486).  The
        probe checks the pinned fpdf2's version and disabledTests, then builds it
        unpatched; it clears once the pin ships 2.9.0, deselects the test, or the
        suite passes again.

    Add a probe here when a version gate cannot see every way the workaround
    becomes unnecessary (as with fpdf2), or when only a real build can tell
    whether upstream is fixed.
